      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "====================\n\nTo find the average value of the given set of numbers, we first need to add up all the values and then divide by the total number of values.\n\nLet's add up the values:\n\n\\[ 0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z \\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[ 0 + (2 + 4 + 8 + 16)z \\]\n\nSum the coefficients:\n\n\\[ 0 + 30z \\]\n\nNow, to find the average, we divide this sum by the total number of values:\n\n\\[ \\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Sum}}{\\text{Count}} \\]\n\nCounting the numbers gives us 5. So, we divide the sum by 5:\n\n\\[ \\text{Average} = \\frac{30z}{5} \\]\n\nSimplifying:\n\n\\[ \\text{Average} = 6z \\]\n\nSo, the average value of $0$, $2z$, $4z$, $8z$, and $16z$ is $\\boxed{6z}$.",
